// THE FOOD COURT — LIBRARY FUNK — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// THE FOOD COURT as a 1974 library / crime-show funk cue — a game alternate of hub, selectable
// from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Peter: "some groovy new remixes for the food court". LIBRARY FUNK is the mall on its opening day
// in 1974, scored off a KPM / De Wolfe / Bruton library record — Lalo Schifrin, "Shaft",
// "Starsky & Hutch": a wah-wah rhythm guitar, a muted funk chop, the clavinet, the tune on flute and
// vibes in unison, a fat fingered bass, a tight kit with open hats, brass punches, strings swelling.
// 
// THE TUNE is THE FOOD COURT's own lead (hub.js section 6) note for note, at three speeds that get
// quicker through the cue: ×4 (quarters) the brass fanfare, ×2 (eighths) the heads, B and the shout,
// ×1 (its own sixteenths) the bass in the breakdown and the whole band in unison for the tag.
// THE HARMONY is the hub's, one chord per cell of its arpeggio:
//   A  | Am9 | Gmaj9 | Am9 | G6 · E7♭9 |       B (a fourth up)  | Dm9 | Cmaj9 | Dm9 | C6 · A7♭9 |
//   build Fmaj7♯11 → E7♯9 (♭VI–V); ending Am9 · F9 · E7♯9 → A minor (major 9th).
// THE LANDMARKS: 90 bpm (the Trophy Room's toaster parade dances at hub.js's bpm); an 8-bar intro
// heard on the walk-in, then the loop from bar 9 (hub.js's loop start), no select loop; no TNGR-2
// or CRLS-1 (the Food Court entry warms MRDR-3 / worklet lanes only); the bass on `bass`.
// 
//   1–2    THE GRAND OPENING — the brass play the tune's first two cells as quarter notes (×4) over a string swell and the timpani; a drum fill into
//   3–4    THE RHYTHM SECTION — the kit (sixteenth hats, open hats on the &s), the fat fingered bass and the wah guitar's scratch on an Am9 vamp
//   5–8    THE BAND — the clavinet and the muted chop come in on the A changes; brass punches; a tom fill into the loop
//   9–16   HEAD A (the loop starts) — the tune in eighths (×2) on flute and vibes in unison; from 13 the flute an octave up, the brass punching the phrase ends
//   17–24  HEAD B — the tune a fourth up in D minor, the string section swelling under it, ride cymbal, the wah back in at 21; its last cell is the hub's own B D F D, into
//   25–28  THE BREAKDOWN — drums and bass take it: the bass plays the tune at its own sixteenth speed (×1), a sine under its roots, the kit on eighth hats
//   29–30  THE DRUM BREAK — the kit alone: ghost notes, open hats, a tom fill
//   31–32  THE BUILD — the crime-funk ♭VI–V: Fmaj7♯11 → E7♯9, strings and brass swelling, the bass pedalling, a snare roll, the wah back in, the timpani rolling into
//   33–40  THE SHOUT — the tune in eighths on the brass in octaves (the hub's octave and the one above), the flute on the top octave, the vibes under; the full band; from 37 the strings sing the tune's top notes over it
//   41–42  THE TAG — the whole band in unison on the tune at its own sixteenth speed (×1): flute, vibes, brass, clav and bass in octaves
//   43–44  THE BIG ENDING — Am9 · F9 · E7♯9 hits, then the A minor (major 9th) spy chord held over a timpani roll; the drummer's pickup turns back to bar 9
// 
// Sounds: the flute (mrdrConcertFlute, exciter) and vibes (mrdrVibraphone) in unison or octaves;
// GUITAR 1 the wah (mrdrWahGuitar, double-stops in sixteenths, spring reverb, the one MRDR-3 guitar);
// GUITAR 2 frppFunkMuted chop (Alternate strum, down-strokes on the eighths, up-strokes 4 dB under,
// parity asserted); the clav (bestPwmClav, the one PWM voice); the brass section (layerBrassStack) for
// the fanfare, the shout and the ending, its punches on mrdrHornStab; the string section
// (frppStringSection) swelling, and singing the tune's top notes in the last shout; the bass
// frppBassBridge over a sine; a tight kit (breakbeat kick, hats and toms, snareWiresTight, ghost
// snares), tambourine, a ride in B; two song-local timpani tuned to A and E.
// 
// Levels set by solo measurement in the shout (bars 33–40) against the remix targets; see the generator.
// Trailing master gain -7.1 dB for −24 LUFS integrated (the hub's menu line).
// 44 bars at 90, swing 55, 117 s; the loop 9–44 is 96 s.
